3. Meaning of the main terms
Term	Plain-English meaning
SaaS	Software businesses use as an online service.
B2B	The customers are businesses.
Tenant / organization	One customer business whose data must remain separate from every other business.
Frontend	The website users interact with.
API / backend	Server code handling authorized requests, business rules, and data.
Monorepo	One repository containing several related applications and shared packages.
Voice worker	A separate program handling live voice conversations.
STT	Speech-to-text: converting the caller’s audio into words.
LLM	The language model that decides what the assistant should say.
TTS	Text-to-speech: converting the assistant’s response into audio.
Streaming	Sending and processing small pieces continuously instead of waiting for the whole response.
VAD	Voice activity detection: detecting when someone starts or stops speaking.
Endpointing	Deciding that the caller has finished their turn.
Barge-in	The caller interrupts while the AI is speaking.
Full duplex	Both sides can send audio at the same time.
LiveKit	The room and real-time media infrastructure connecting participants and agents.
WebRTC	Technology used to transport real-time browser audio.
WebSocket	A persistent connection used to exchange streaming messages or audio.
PCM16	Raw audio represented by signed 16-bit samples.
Sample rate	The number of audio samples per second, such as 16,000 Hz.
Resampling	Actually converting audio between sample rates.
Backpressure	Preventing a fast producer from overwhelming a slower consumer or filling memory.
SIP / PSTN	Technologies involved in connecting software voice systems to ordinary telephone calls.
CDR	A provider’s call-detail record, including authoritative call timing information.
ORM	A library for working with database records from application code.
Migration	A versioned, reviewable database structure change.
RLS	Database row-level security, used here to isolate organizations.
Ledger	An append-only record of financial entries.
Reservation / hold	Funds temporarily allocated to a call before the final charge is known.
Settlement	Calculating the final charge and resolving the reservation.
Idempotency	Ensuring retries or duplicate events do not repeat an action or charge.
Reconciliation	Checking uncertain local state against authoritative provider information.
p95 latency	A latency threshold that 95% of measured samples fall at or below.
Mocked test	A test using simulated providers or components.
Live provider test	A test that actually contacts the external service.


