12.3 Make interruptions reliable
When the caller starts speaking:
1. Detect speech locally.
2. Invalidate the obsolete response generation.
3. Cancel its LLM stream.
4. Cancel its TTS stream.
5. Stop pending audio forwarding.
6. Clear queued playback.
7. Reject late results from the old generation.
8. Respond to the new caller turn.
